 "notes": [
  "Per-step percentiles are the median of Locust's rolling 10-second percentiles over the step's steady part (its first 30 s are skipped as ramp-up).",
  "Locust rounds times for its percentiles (to 10 ms above 100 ms, to 100 ms above 1 s), so a p99 can read slightly above the slowest request.",
  "CPU is the app process as % of ONE core (one async worker, plus threads for bcrypt); PostgreSQL is the database container's CPU %.",
  "Rate-limited answers (HTTP 429 from the comment and AI limits) are protections working and are counted as successes under their own name.",
  "The AI tutor's timings (first word, whole streamed answer) are measured separately and are not part of the request statistics: an answer that streams for many seconds is not a page load. Opening the answer stream is a normal request.",
  "Database CPU is missing for the first 4 minutes of this run. The first resource sampler read the wrong container (a bug in the test tooling, now fixed), so its database figures were thrown away; its app CPU and memory are kept until the corrected sampler took over.",
  "This is the second full run. The first one, with uvicorn's default 5-second keep-alive, lost 73 of about 31,500 requests (0.23 %) to connection resets, all at 300-400 users. None of the 3,600+ requests sent straight after another response (sign-in, the calendar feed, video progress) failed, which is the signature of an idle connection being closed just as it is reused. Keep-alive is now 75 s (KEEP_ALIVE_SECONDS); with the same load this run had no failures."
 ]
